# ─── 4. DATA — runtime state, not source ─────────────────────────────────
# The canonical runtime root is `data/`. One thing under it is tracked source
# and has to stay reachable: the investigation-queue marker. Everything else
# in there is runtime.
#
# `!/data/test-fixtures/` is still a NAMED rule — the platform-invariance guard
# names it explicitly, and a named rule is a rule somebody can reason about
# instead of an accident of ordering. §9 excludes the directory itself now (the
# fixtures belonged to the store that is Postgres now), and the last rule to
# match decides: the exclusion wins.
#
# The ORDER is what makes it work, and the last rule to match is the one that
# decides. `/data/*` matches the directory ITSELF — its `*` matches the empty
# remainder — and a directory git excludes is one it never descends into, so
# a file re-included beneath it stays invisible. `!/data/` therefore comes
# AFTER `/data/*`: it is then the last rule that matches the directory, the
# directory is reachable, and git descends far enough to see the negations
# inside it. The leading slash matters: without it the rule also matched
# `src/ikigai/data/`.
/data/*
!/data/
!/data/investigation_queue/
/data/investigation_queue/*
!/data/investigation_queue/.keep
!/data/test-fixtures/
/data/*.db
/data/*.json
/data/*.jsonl
/data/chroma_db/
/data/*.log
/data/session-*.md
/data/*-sessions/
/data/pytest-tmp/
# The store layer is PUBLISHED (ADR-037 D4): the pool and the repository are
# the only code that talks to the driver. `/src/data/` excluded the whole
# DIRECTORY, and that also killed the negations under it — git never
# descends into a directory it excluded, so a file re-included beneath an
# excluded parent stays invisible. The directory is left alone here; only its
# junk is ignored, and the four real files are named back.
/src/data/*
!/src/data/__init__.py
!/src/data/AGENTS.md
!/src/data/client.py
!/src/data/repository.py
# The drafts: the persistence of the prose a client is still writing (ADR-040).
# It was MISSING from this list while `src/services/drafts.py` imported it, so
# the module existed on the owner's disk and in no clone — the service raised
# ImportError for everyone else while the suite here was green. A deny-all rule
# under a directory is a rule that every new file has to be named back into.
!/src/data/drafts.py
/src/data/ikigai_checkpoints.db
/src/ikigai/data/
/src/ikigai/vault/
/tests/data/pytest-tmp/
/vibe-ops/**/*.db
/vibe-ops/chroma_db/

